{
  "id": "how-it-works",
  "format": "diagram",
  "height": 560,
  "title": "How stackledger publishes a catalogue",
  "description": "Flowchart. On your Mac, stackledger discover writes a snapshot that stays on the Mac, and drift --scaffold helps you edit catalog/*.yaml. A git push sends the catalogue to a private GitHub repository. A pull request runs gitleaks, validate and build but never deploys. A push to main runs gitleaks, validate and build with stackledger from the npm registry, then wrangler pages deploy publishes the whole static site to Cloudflare Pages, which never reads GitHub. A reader reaches Pages only through Cloudflare Access, signing in first. Personal mode: the full site only, one Access application for the owner, / leads to /full/. Corporate mode: full and staff sites, finance on /full/*, staff on the rest, / leads to /staff/.",
